<metadata><name>White River Glacier Moraines</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:183-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.303657" lon="-121.674434"><ele>1305.0</ele><name>White River West Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:white-river-west-sno-park (OSM way 40773253); confidence: high; pdf_page: 185; book_elev_ft: 4223; quote: From White River West Sno-Park ski up the valley.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.328560" lon="-121.695970"><ele>1590.3</ele><name>Foot of the White River Glacier moraines</name><desc>source: OSM White River line 2.15 mi above the bridge, where the DEM reaches 5,220 ft (start + the book's 980 ft); the Timberline side valley comes in from the west here; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 185; book_elev_ft: 5200; quote: Along the 2-mile ascent ... to the foot of giant moraines ... Near the moraines, you will see on the south side of the valley a short, almost bowl-like side valley. This is the route leading to or from Timberline Lodge, only a mile farther.</desc></wpt>
